          <startedAt>2026-09-01T20:47:14</startedAt>
          <baseCommit>02dd2db01864e740fb61b32f0157e8be6743ffd6</baseCommit>
          <output>Stage 2 modified exactly one model file: blocks/org/blockml/bml/workspace/playground/PoemNew.bml. Execute replaced the German poem with a Russian translation: (1) the &lt;is> line now reads 'translated into Russian from German, about a tree and a mushroom'; (2) all four stanzas in &lt;documentation> were rewritten in Russian, preserving the four-quatrain structure, the tree/mushroom subjects, and the beech's spoken passage; (3) the properties/title/value changed from 'Im Schatten der Buche' to 'В тени бука'. The author value ('John Doe') and the block name/type/baseType were left unchanged. No ModelTransformation or _meta/transform/ files were touched, and no other files were modified. The change is self-contained and consistent with a German→Russian translation stage; recommend running `npx blockml validate` to confirm the block still parses (core:Documentation baseType, unchanged structure — expected to pass).</output>
